{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline","id":1132471,"title":"The Heirs of Odin: A Ventrue Bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-21T19:27:48-07:00","id":1132471,"title":"The Heirs of Odin: A Ventrue Bloodline","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>So, after spending some time on these forums and rarely contributing any material I\u2019ve decided to give a shot at some homebrew material. These first few bloodlines I will be writing will be based upon Norse Mythology, but if all goes well (if people like what I put out) I will delve into other inspirations.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>So here we go, the Heirs of Odin.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cOur great forefather was blessed by the Lord of Asgard; Lord Odin gave unto us his many gifts, and you shall know them most painfully.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Heirs of Odin; it sounds arrogant to name yourself after a god, but for the Ventrue it is par for the course.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">History: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Heirs of Odin often tell that their founder was blessed by Odin to help fight the forces of Ragnarok. After all, mortal servants have time as their eternal enemy, and they soon grow withered and frail: the immortal Kindred, on the other hand, have time as their ally in their war, and they only grow stronger with time.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Covenants: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Heirs of Odin are often found within the Circle of the Crone; this covenant brings an army of blood sorcerers in service to the ancient gods, so the Heirs of Odin often feel comfortable here in both practicality and spirituality.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Heirs of Odin more often than not oppose the Ordo Dracul; while the Ordo Dracul would be a useful ally when the Heirs of Odin fight the forces of Ragnarok, but it is their philosophy that puts the two at odds. The Ordo Dracul have a mission statement of defying the gods by changing their nature, and some Ordo Dracul have the outright intention of knocking the gods off their thrones, and by doing so Ragnarok will occur.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Becoming: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A potential Heir of Odin must offer the Bloodline some advantage with staving off Ragnarok; whether this be a large access to supplies, great shamanic knowledge and abilities, or by being a great warrior. The Heirs of Odin have no time for the weak and useless.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Clan: Ventrue</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nickname: Odin\u2019s Hall, Odinsons</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Disciplines: Dominate, Animalism, Resilience, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Auspex</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bloodline Bane: The Heirs of Odin are relentless in their pursuits; in fact, they must be. A Heir of Odin that doesn\u2019t work towards their current goals will begin taking a negative one penalty towards resisting frenzy each night they remain inactive. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once the Heir of Odin reaches a chance die they will automatically frenzy with no option of resisting: they must either ride the wave or succumb. After this frenzy the Heir of Odin lose all penalties to resisting, but the cycle will continue if they don't pursue their current goals.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Torpor does not apply any penalties to the Heir of Odin once they awaken.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bloodline Gift: The Gift of Shamans</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Much like Odin, his heirs are often Shamans as well. The Heir of Odin receives an honorary Spirit Rank equal to half his blood potency rounded down.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Heir of Odin may spend a vitae to see spirits within the twilight, and their Discipline of Animalism works on these Animistic entities so long as said entity does not represent one of the Kindred\u2019s banes.<br /> <br /> <i>So there we have it. Like it, hate it, your choice. I would appreciate some criticism on the matter before I put out the other bloodlines, but please make it constructive criticism. Oh, and if you have any questions on why I did any of the stuff above then please just ask in the thread. I'll try to get you an answer when I can.</i></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","user":"Ever Professional","date":".  Grammar. 08-21-2017, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T19:42:30-07:00","id":1132473,"title":"","content":"Very cool idea! I love the honorary spirit rank as a bloodline gift for vampires!<br /> <br /> One question/suggestion though... and I really don't mean to offend with it. Is there any other possible name you could give them? Heirs of Odin? Odinsons? I ask because the Sons of Odin, at least in Canada, is an anti-immigration group that spews hateful crap at anyone they deem not to be &quot;Western.&quot; I have absolutely zero doubt that the names are 100% coincidence. I just cringe whenever I hear &quot;Sons of Odin&quot; these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T20:08:20-07:00","id":1132479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132473#post1132473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very cool idea! I love the honorary spirit rank as a bloodline gift for vampires!<br /> <br /> One question/suggestion though... and I really don't mean to offend with it. Is there any other possible name you could give them? Heirs of Odin? Odinsons? I ask because the Sons of Odin, at least in Canada, is an anti-immigration group that spews hateful crap at anyone they deem not to be &quot;Western.&quot; I have absolutely zero doubt that the names are 100% coincidence. I just cringe whenever I hear &quot;Sons of Odin&quot; these days.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh my god, I didn't know that. Yeah, they can totally have a different name. I just went with Sons of Odin because it was the first thing that popped in my head. But yeah, they can totally have a different name. I'm an American, so I really don't know much about canadian stuff despite living relatively close to it. So yeah, I'll definitely change the name. Thanks for telling me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T20:14:40-07:00","id":1132483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132479#post1132479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh my god, I didn't know that. Yeah, they can totally have a different name. I just went with Sons of Odin because it was the first thing that popped in my head. But yeah, they can totally have a different name. I'm an American, so I really don't know much about canadian stuff despite living relatively close to it. So yeah, I'll definitely change the name. Thanks for telling me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely no worries. It is a good, logical name for a Bloodline, it just happened to have already been stolen by a group of people who &quot;swear they aren't racist.&quot; Honestly, if I wasn't a news junkie and if this didn't hit particularly close to home for me, I may not have known about it either. <br /> <br /> Anyhow... really cool idea, awesome mechanics, and very evocative mythology! I hope you get time to expand on them!","