ategory/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132553#post1132553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mmm... not sure how Animalism can work on spirits, considering many of them (rank 2 and above) are sapient beings albeit aliens in their perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first three levels animalism are just for animals. Levels four and five allow for tapping into that primal thought in humans, Kindred, and other supernaturals. I could limit it to Animistic spirits, seeing as that was the primary goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T06:34:15-07:00","id":1132583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132553#post1132553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mmm... not sure how Animalism can work on spirits, considering many of them (rank 2 and above) are sapient beings albeit aliens in their perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>May be so, but even more specifically, Spirits are <i>predators</i>. I'd allow it on that basis alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T08:54:00-07:00","id":1132640,"title":"","content":"Edit: Nevermind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T09:33:21-07:00","id":1132658,"title":"","content":"It seems we think alike, I'm working on a Mekhet bloodline that combines Animalism and Auspex to commune with spirits.<br /> I can't remember if I had any other good ideas but one devotion was Auspex 3 Animalism 1 to make a offer where a spirit gets the Vitae spent on the devotion as Essence and if they fail to keep their end of the deal they suffer a level of Vinculum, what behaviour this breeds is questionable as you're dealing with spirits who might express their affection in any number of ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T09:54:39-07:00","id":1132677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132583#post1132583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May be so, but even more specifically, Spirits are <i>predators</i>. I'd allow it on that basis alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are humans, and yet a Gangrel cannot use Feral Whispers on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T10:03:20-07:00","id":1132680,"title":"","content":"This is a very interesting bloodline and I'd like to hear more about how they originated, etc. --they could be quite old, much as the Childer of The Morrigan are represented. Their bloodline gift and bane are both viable and not confining, which to me makes them a more eminently playable bloodline. I may very well find a use for them in my own, dark eras campaign.<br /> <br /> Side note: VtM has an NPC vamp elder, a Gangrel, called the All-High, who is/was basically Odin and vanished before the Middle Ages in Scandinavia. If the Heirs of Odin are linked to an Odin-like founder, then what other Nordic/Germanic (Heirs of Wodin) bloodlines might be out there? Perhaps long ago an entire court, or Covenant, of &quot;Asgardian&quot; kindred flourished, and now lies sleeping, forgotten beneath frozen Thule....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T10:34:10-07:00","id":1132689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132677#post1132677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So are humans, and yet a Gangrel cannot use Feral Whispers on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't really need to use Feral Whispers on a human. Gangrel can already talk to people, and various skills can be used to convince people to do something for you.<br /> <br /> However, part of the reason I have animalism affect spirits is because Odin did have shamanic capabilities, and spirits in Norse Mythology are typically more animistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T10:43:16-07:00","id":1132693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132689#post1132689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and spirits in Norse Mythology are typically more animistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Animistic is not the same thing as animalistic, and while many Norse spirits are animistic, I haven't personally heard much about any animal-like spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T10:49:42-07:00","id":1132694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132680#post1132680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very interesting bloodline and I'd like to hear more about how they originated, etc. --they could be quite old, much as the Childer of The Morrigan are represented. Their bloodline gift and bane are both viable and not confining, which to me makes them a more eminently playable bloodline. I may very well find a use for them in my own, dark eras campaign.<br /> <br /> Side note: VtM has an NPC vamp elder, a Gangrel, called the All-High, who is/was basically Odin and vanished before the Middle Ages in Scandinavia. If the Heirs of Odin are linked to an Odin-like founder, then what other Nordic/Germanic (Heirs of Wodin) bloodlines might be out there? Perhaps long ago an entire court, or Covenant, of &quot;Asgardian&quot; kindred flourished, and now lies sleeping, forgotten beneath frozen Thule....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'm happy you like the bloodline, and I hope you get some fun out of it. I would have put how old they are, but I didn't want to feel like anyone was limited by. My preferred interpretation is that they've been around for awhile, but they have resurgences during large global wars.<br /> <br /> This bloodline is partially inspired by the All High, but I decided to go with Ventrue because they evoke more of a Lordly tone, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> I actually am trying to design Nordic/Germanic bloodlines for the other main clans (and possibly the Lost Clans as well).<br /> <br /> Currently I am working on a Gangrel bloodline inspired by Loki. He was a notorious shapeshifter, much like the Clan themselves. I'm debating on how I want to design their trickster role, so it might take a bit.<br /> <br /> I also have plans to delve into other mythologies for vampire bloodlines. I personally love mythology, so I'll probably delve into some Roman or Greek mythology after I finish up the Nordic/Germanic ones. I do have a friend who knows more about shinto than I do, so I plan to consult him on making bloodlines eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T10:51:55-07:00","id":1132696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132693#post1132693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Animistic is not the same thing as animalistic, and while many Norse spirits are animistic, I haven't personally heard much about any animal-like spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do have a fair point. I do want them to have something to do with spirits though because of Odin's shamanistic aspects, so what would you suggest in that aspect? Design a few bloodline specific Cruac rituals for that, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T11:02:23-07:00","id":1132705,"title":"","content":"You mean besides Huginn, Munin, and Sleipnir? The concept of animal spirits and family totem animals were major components of Norse religious practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T12:08:00-07:00","id":1132736,"title":"","content":"Personally I wouldn't worry about further limiting their ability to interact with spirits, by specifying the type thereof. That ultimately just makes more work for the Storyteller and is redundant since <i>ALL</i> CofD spirits are violent, predatory things that should be salted, burned with fire and buried at a crossroads... er, *cough*, ehem. I mean creepy and predatory, yeah. That happiness spirit is totally cool with you... at least until it gets hungry.<br /> <br /> I don't think these guys need special Cruac rituals or anything, since being treated as a certain Rank and having a means to communicate across the gauntlet AND command spirits gives them <i><b>ENORMOUS</b></i> power. Basically, think of the Heirs of Odin as being VtM's Giovanni bloodline, who were so out there with necromancy they got a whole chronicle book treatment around their ability to attack/influence/spy on the living and undead at a distance, using ghosts as proxies. Only here it's spirits.... and the Heir just has to ensure they are properly &quot;paid&quot; in essence. Yeah....<br /> <br /> They'll either get long very well with some werewolves--and spirits, or have a highly, highly contentious relationship, depending.<br /> <br /> So, it's the elegance unfolding into complexity that attracts me.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> Edit: I totally get this bloodline as Ventrue in the CofD. Ventrue have animalism, they rule, and prior to the Fall of the Camarilla were a kind of feral tribal chief/king group forced to the barbarian side by the Julii Rome. (At least in Europe.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 08-22-2017, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T12:48:56-07:00","id":1132751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132736#post1132736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I wouldn't worry about further limiting their ability to interact with spirits, by specifying the type thereof. That ultimately just makes more work for the Storyteller and is redundant since <i>ALL</i> CofD spirits are violent, predatory things that should be salted, burned with fire and buried at a crossroads... er, *cough*, ehem. I mean creepy and predatory, yeah. That happiness spirit is totally cool with you... at least until it gets hungry.<br /> <br /> I don't think these guys need special Cruac rituals or anything, since being treated as a certain Rank and having a means to communicate across the gauntlet AND command spirits gives them <i><b>ENORMOUS</b></i> power. Basically, think of the Heirs of Odin as being VtM's Giovanni bloodline, who were so out there with necromancy they got a whole chronicle book treatment around their ability to attack/influence/spy on the living and undead at a distance, using ghosts as proxies. Only here it's spirits.... and the Heir just has to ensure they are properly &quot;paid&quot; in essence. Yeah....<br /> <br /> They'll either get long very well with some werewolves--and spirits, or have a highly, highly contentious relationship, depending.<br /> <br /> So, it's the elegance unfolding into complexity that attracts me.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> Edit: I totally get this bloodline as Ventrue in the CofD. Ventrue have animalism, they rule, and prior to the Fall of the Camarilla were a kind of feral tribal chief/king group forced to the barbarian side by the Julii Rome. (At least in Europe.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I disagree. Precisely because their ability is so powerful among the kindred (not so much against mages or werewolves), I would restrict it to several spirit types or chorus. Maybe making them buy each one (crow, horse) as separate specialities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T14:10:45-07:00","id":1132798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132751#post1132751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I disagree. Precisely because their ability is so powerful among the kindred (not so much against mages or werewolves), I would restrict it to several spirit types or chorus. Maybe making them buy each one (crow, horse) as separate specialities.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got a fair point as well. So, possibly making some Animalism devotions instead of an outright ability, or having the Heir of Odin choose a specific animal as his specialty in the spirit realm?<br /> <br /> I'm always up for suggestions on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T14:37:21-07:00","id":1132808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132705#post1132705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean besides Huginn, Munin, and Sleipnir? The concept of animal spirits and family totem animals were major components of Norse religious practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually part of why I chose animalism. There were quite a few various Norse mythological figures that were animals or resembled animals in some way, but it might work out if I just limit the Animalism as spirit powers to Animalistic spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T21:39:15-07:00","id":1132907,"title":"","content":"<i>Okay, in response to the suggestions I'm putting out a merit for the Heirs of Odin to act as an optional rule for their bloodline advantage. As previously stated, please send suggestions to me on how to alter and make this as well-written as possible.</i> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><i><b>Gift of the Shaman (0,000, and 000)</b></i></u><br /> <br /> Description: The Odinson deals with and fights against forces within this realm and the next, and the Animalistic Spirits had been the allies of the Shamans of old; this still holds true for the Heirs of Odin into these modern nights. The Heir of Odin gains the first dot of this merit once they join the bloodline.<br /> <br /> 0- The Heirs of Odin must be able to fight the forces of Ragnarok on all fronts; for this purpose the ancient warriors blessed by Odin have passed down the gift to peer into the frequency of twilight that houses Spirits. The Heir of Odin gains an honorary spiritual rank equal to half his blood potency (rounded down), and is also able to use Feral Whispers on spirits of rank equal to his.<br /> <br /> 000- The Heirs of Odin often take spiritual companions from the spiritual twilight much like Odin himself did. The Heir of Odin chooses a type of spirit (normally wolves or ravens, but more occult-minded Heirs have taken spirits of Cold or Winter as their companions). The Heir of Odin is able to house their chosen spirit type in an animal they have raised with Raise the Familiar, and they may use Summon the Hunt in regards to the spiritual type they have chosen.<br /> <br /> 00000- The penultimate might of the Heir of Odin. The Heir of Odin may now affect spirits with Feral Injection, but as supernatural entities Spirits may spend willpower to resist the vampires commands. When the Heir of Odin uses Lord of the Land, their territory not only affects this realm, but the spiritual realm as well. Spirits are affected by Lord of the Land, but the Discipline abilities that work on said spirits do not change.<br /> <br /> Some powerful Heirs have claimed to use their territory to travel to a realm that is like a Shadow to our own, and it is the home that all spirits travel from.</span></span> <hr /><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">So yeah, I know it probably isn't the best alteration, but I still find it to be a pretty neat one. Anyway, tell me how y'all like the merit, and what I need to alter to actually make it viable.</span></span></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","user":"Ever Professional","date":". 08-23-2017, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T02:33:39-07:00","id":1132950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132907#post1132907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Heir of Odin is able to house their chosen spirit type in an animal they have raised with Raise the Familiar</div> </div> </div> </div>What Manifestation would that be? Possession? Claim? Something custom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T05:57:06-07:00","id":1132979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1132950#post1132950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What Manifestation would that be? Possession? Claim? Something custom?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I would go with the Possessed condition because Raise the Familiar is not a permament power, but if you wanted to use the Claimed condition for added fun with werewolves, go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T11:18:03-07:00","id":1133093,"title":"","content":"First, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2411\" data-vbnamecard=\"2411\">Raistlin</a> is correct. And I recognize that by the time my previous post was finished I'd effectively highlighted why their power set should be limited.<br /> <br /> Second, the Merit listed looks like an excellent way of handling the intended interactions. You could perhaps use a custom Devotion to enter Twilight, utilizing Animalism and Dominate to take control of a spirit, perhaps? That way the Odinsons do not physically cross the gauntlet, but are still able to travel the spirit-world in a kind of dream-state. <br /> <br /> Third, why not simply apply the Open condition to the target of Raise the Familiar? If the vampire has properly coordinated the first and most available spirit will be the one he wants--one with Fetter... if not, then hilarity may ensue. You'll have the familiar Ridden, then Claimed, but it will take time to integrate and the vamp will need to ensure a flow of essence so this won't be an instant-Huginn kind of thing. <br /> <br /> Note that if you make a direct path to claimed the spirit technically can animate the &quot;familiar&quot; long after Raise has ended--it's now a claimed object and while likely twisting the spirit into magath (have fun explaining yourself to Forsaken) the claim can persist until something snaps the spirit out.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T11:29:53-07:00","id":1133094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1133093#post1133093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll have the familiar Ridden, then Claimed</div> </div> </div> </div>Small nitpick: Ridden is the collective term for Urged, Possessed and Claimed in second edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 08-24-2017, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T04:32:18-07:00","id":1133320,"title":"","content":"I arrive late to the party, but i wanted to tell you that i have loved your Bloodline. Very nice concept, really nicely tied to Odin's themes and his Ragnarok obsession. I would have maybe gone with some Rune magic as the Bloodline gift, but yours is more elegant (great job at designing the Merit, btw) and original, for all that matters. Nice job! The Bloodline Bane is just the same of one Bloodline of mine, some sneaky shapeshifters-dopplegangers obsessed with knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T09:19:58-07:00","id":1133412,"title":"","content":"Really digging this bloodline. Spirits are always a fun way to make things <i>&quot;interesting&quot;</i>, and the Norse trappings add a nice flair.<br /> If I can throw my two cents in on the &quot;Raise the Familiar&quot; thing? I'd personally be inclined to run it as (like previously suggested) tagging the Familiar as Open for the appropriate spirits, <b>but</b> also allowing the Familiar to be considered a &quot;living&quot; host for the purposes of the Claim Manifestation so long as the vampire maintains it with Vitae. At storyteller discretion this may subject the spirit to a blood bond, but it gets a more stable and durable body out of the deal, and the vampire gets a more potent and intelligent familiar with a couple weird powers. Although as an intelligent entity, the Claimed familiar should probably be able to resist Feral Whispers... on the other hand, if you allow it to be subjected to a blood bond it may not <i>want</i> to. Trade-offs can be fun.<br /> <br /> (Also, now I kinda want to try spinning a sort of &quot;cousin bloodline&quot; for these, for a smallish story I'm hoping to run down the line. Gangrel instead of Ventrue with the appropriate tweaks to flavor, swapping some control for a little Spirit-Twilight interaction at higher Discipline/Cr\u00faac levels, that sort of thing... would you be alright with me tinkering around with the Heirs to do that, giving my group the link to the original bloodline in the process?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 08-24-2017, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T12:29:22-07:00","id":1133499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1133412#post1133412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really digging this bloodline. Spirits are always a fun way to make things interesting, and the Norse trappings add a nice flair.<br /> If I can throw my two cents in on the Raise the Familiar thing? I'd personally be inclined to run it as (like previously suggested) tagging the Familiar as Open for the appropriate spirits, but also allowing the Familiar to be considered a living host for the purposes of the Claim Manifestation so long as the vampire maintains it with Vitae. At storyteller discretion this may subject the spirit to a blood bond, but it gets a more stable and durable body out of the deal, and the vampire gets a more potent and intelligent familiar with a couple weird powers. Although as an intelligent entity, the Claimed familiar should probably be able to resist Feral Whispers... on the other hand, if you allow it to be subjected to a blood bond it may not want to. Trade-offs can be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm leaning more towards having the Open condition apply towards the power. I've just been looking over all the options before putting it under the merit, and I will keep in mind your idea on the Familiar counting as a living host for Claimed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Also, now I kinda want to try spinning a sort of cousin bloodline for these, for a smallish story I'm hoping to run down the line. Gangrel instead of Ventrue with the appropriate tweaks to flavor, swapping some control for a little Spirit-Twilight interaction at higher Discipline/Cr\u00faac levels, that sort of thing... would you be alright with me tinkering around with the Heirs to do that, giving my group the link to the original bloodline in the process?) </div> </div> </div>Sure, I don't mind you tinkering around with it for your own games. Not like I could stop you, anyway. And if you give your players the link to this bloodline, that'd be cool. They might have suggestions on how to make it better, or they might want to use it for their own games at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T14:29:25-07:00","id":1133547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1132471-the-heirs-of-odin-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=1133499#post1133499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, I don't mind you tinkering around with it for your own games. Not like I could stop you, anyway. And if you give your players the link to this bloodline, that'd be cool. They might have suggestions on how to make it better, or they might want to use it for their own games at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, awesome, thanks. Given folks' interest in vampires and spirits, the bloodline and anything related to them should be a solid fit at our table. And if they have any questions or ideas I'll send 'em this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}